{
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.1,
   "text": "If you pitch a tent in your backyard,"
  },
  {
   "start": 1.3,
   "end": 3.44,
   "text": "throw Kevin inside and charge him $20 to sleep there."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.58,
   "end": 4.88,
   "text": "Congratulations, you've built a hotel."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.06,
   "end": 7.6,
   "text": "A hotel with zero stars and approximately 4,000 mosquitoes."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.92,
   "end": 9.22,
   "text": "Kevin crawls inside, lies down,"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.36,
   "end": 10.62,
   "text": "and immediately gets bitten on the forehead."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.76,
   "end": 11.36,
   "text": "Then it starts raining."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.56,
   "end": 12.66,
   "text": "The roof leaks, the floor floods,"
  },
  {
   "start": 12.84,
   "end": 14.12,
   "text": "and Kevin wakes up floating on his mattress."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.34,
   "end": 15.68,
   "text": "He screams, why is my bed swimming?"
  },
  {
   "start": 15.86,
   "end": 17.16,
   "text": "Because you booked the Titanic, Kevin!"
  },
  {
   "start": 17.32,
   "end": 19.1,
   "text": "So you build solid walls and a waterproof roof."
  },
  {
   "start": 19.32,
   "end": 21.0,
   "text": "Now Kevin stays dry, but there's another problem."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.1,
   "end": 22.06,
   "text": "The tent doesn't have a bathroom."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.2,
   "end": 23.0,
   "text": "Kevin walks into the garden."
  },
  {
   "start": 23.22,
   "end": 24.74,
   "text": "Grandma sees him and throws a shoe at his head."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.86,
   "end": 25.88,
   "text": "So you install indoor plumbing,"
  },
  {
   "start": 26.0,
   "end": 26.96,
   "text": "toilets, and proper drainage."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.2,
   "end": 28.22,
   "text": "Now Kevin can use the bathroom"
  },
  {
   "start": 28.22,
   "end": 29.3,
   "text": "without becoming a neighborhood criminal."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.3,
   "end": 30.38,
   "text": "But he wants a hot shower."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.58,
   "end": 31.4,
   "text": "So you install a water heater"
  },
  {
   "start": 31.4,
   "end": 32.68,
   "text": "and pipes that supply hot water."
  },
  {
   "start": 32.96,
   "end": 33.56,
   "text": "Now Kevin can shower."
  },
  {
   "start": 33.72,
   "end": 35.44,
   "text": "Unfortunately, he uses all the hot water."
  },
  {
   "start": 35.58,
   "end": 36.7,
   "text": "The next guest walks in, screams,"
  },
  {
   "start": 36.92,
   "end": 38.2,
   "text": "and comes out looking like a frozen chicken."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.42,
   "end": 39.48,
   "text": "So you upgrade the hot water system"
  },
  {
   "start": 39.48,
   "end": 40.42,
   "text": "to serve multiple rooms."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.6,
   "end": 41.74,
   "text": "But now more people wanna stay."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.9,
   "end": 42.7,
   "text": "So you make the building bigger."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.88,
   "end": 44.74,
   "text": "10 rooms, 50 rooms, 200 rooms."
  },
  {
   "start": 45.02,
   "end": 47.12,
   "text": "Now you need elevators, fire exits, and a reception desk."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.3,
   "end": 48.26,
   "text": "Kevin becomes the receptionist."
  },
  {
   "start": 48.36,
   "end": 49.72,
   "text": "The first guest asks, do you have any vacancies?"
  },
  {
   "start": 49.98,
   "end": 50.86,
   "text": "Kevin says, what's a vacancy?"
  },
  {
   "start": 51.1,
   "end": 52.1,
   "text": "Bro, you have one job!"
  },
  {
   "start": 52.26,
   "end": 54.24,
   "text": "So you hire actual staff and install a booking system."
  },
  {
   "start": 54.4,
   "end": 55.74,
   "text": "Now guests can reserve rooms online."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.92,
   "end": 57.54,
   "text": "But Kevin wants a swimming pool, so you build one."
  },
  {
   "start": 57.66,
   "end": 58.88,
   "text": "Then he wants a gym, so you build one."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.88,
   "end": 59.68,
   "text": "Then he wants a restaurant."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.88,
   "end": 61.58,
   "text": "So you hire chefs and install a professional kitchen."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.16,
   "end": 63.16,
   "text": "Unfortunately, Kevin becomes the head chef."
  },
  {
   "start": 63.32,
   "end": 64.7,
   "text": "His first dish, microwaved cereal."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.84,
   "end": 66.74,
   "text": "The restaurant loses three Michelin stars it never had."
  },
  {
   "start": 66.9,
   "end": 68.2,
   "text": "So you replace him with someone who understands"
  },
  {
   "start": 68.2,
   "end": 69.2,
   "text": "that milk is not a soup."
  },
  {
   "start": 69.34,
   "end": 70.68,
   "text": "Add air conditioning, soundproofing,"
  },
  {
   "start": 70.78,
   "end": 72.18,
   "text": "room service elevators, luxury suites,"
  },
  {
   "start": 72.32,
   "end": 73.42,
   "text": "and an enormous glass entrance."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.88,
   "end": 75.3,
   "text": "Congratulations, you've built a five-star hotel!"
  },
  {
   "start": 75.58,
   "end": 76.06,
   "text": "Celebrities arrive."
  },
  {
   "start": 76.3,
   "end": 77.48,
   "text": "Rich people pay thousands per night."
  },
  {
   "start": 77.64,
   "end": 79.44,
   "text": "Kevin becomes the hotel's first VIP guest."
  },
  {
   "start": 79.58,
   "end": 81.76,
   "text": "He orders champagne, a personal chef, and a golden toilet."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.9,
   "end": 83.18,
   "text": "Everything is perfect, until checkout."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.4,
   "end": 84.34,
   "text": "The receptionist hands him a bill."
  },
  {
   "start": 84.46,
   "end": 85.82,
   "text": "That'll be $47,000, sir."
  },
  {
   "start": 85.94,
   "end": 87.42,
   "text": "Kevin screams, $47,000?"
  },
  {
   "start": 87.52,
   "end": 88.46,
   "text": "You ordered a golden toilet."
  },
  {
   "start": 88.46,
   "end": 89.5,
   "text": "But I own the hotel!"
  },
  {
   "start": 89.74,
   "end": 90.64,
   "text": "The receptionist checks her computer."
  },
  {
   "start": 90.86,
   "end": 91.76,
   "text": "Actually, sir, you don't."
  },
  {
   "start": 91.9,
   "end": 92.3,
   "text": "Kevin freezes."
  },
  {
   "start": 92.64,
   "end": 92.74,
   "text": "What?"
  },
  {
   "start": 92.9,
   "end": 94.36,
   "text": "It belongs to the person who owns this land."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.8,
   "end": 95.9,
   "text": "Suddenly, grandma walks into the lobby,"
  },
  {
   "start": 95.96,
   "end": 97.54,
   "text": "wearing sunglasses, and holding a property deed."
  },
  {
   "start": 97.78,
   "end": 99.02,
   "text": "Thank you for improving my backyard!"
  },
  {
   "start": 99.28,
   "end": 100.62,
   "text": "Kevin looks at the hotel, then at grandma,"
  },
  {
   "start": 100.84,
   "end": 101.42,
   "text": "then at his bill."
  },
  {
   "start": 101.62,
   "end": 102.02,
   "text": "Grandma smiles."
  },
  {
   "start": 102.28,
   "end": 102.92,
   "text": "Would you like to leave a tip?"
  },
  {
   "start": 103.04,
   "end": 105.52,
   "text": "We spent $500 million building a luxury hotel,"
  },
  {
   "start": 105.66,
   "end": 107.1,
   "text": "and grandma still charges Kevin rent."
  }
 ],
